
### Exercise 1 - Get existing event
GET http://localhost:8080/api/events/2

### Exercise 1 - Get non-existing event
GET http://localhost:8080/api/events/999


### Exercise 2 - Get all events (no filter)
GET http://localhost:8080/api/events

### Exercise 2 - Filter Technology events
GET http://localhost:8080/api/events?category=Technology

### Exercise 2 - Filter Education events
GET http://localhost:8080/api/events?category=Education

### Exercise 2 - Filter non-existing category
GET http://localhost:8080/api/events?category=Music

### Exercise 3 - Create event using JSON
POST http://localhost:8080/api/events
Content-Type: application/json
Accept: application/json

{
  "name": "Spring Conference",
  "category": "Technology"
}


### Exercise 4 - Update existing event
PUT http://localhost:8080/api/events/2
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "name": "Advanced Spring Boot Lab",
  "category": "Technology"
}


### Exercise 4 - Update non-existing event
PUT http://localhost:8080/api/events/999
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "name": "Unknown Event",
  "category": "Technology"
}


### Exercise 4 - Delete existing event
DELETE http://localhost:8080/api/events/2


### Exercise 4 - Delete non-existing event
DELETE http://localhost:8080/api/events/999

### Exercise 5 - Request with custom header
GET http://localhost:8080/api/client-info
X-Client: IntelliJ
Accept: application/json


### Exercise 5 - Request without custom header
GET http://localhost:8080/api/client-info
Accept: application/json

